IMPORT prelude

-- Land Tax Act 2000 (Tas), with the Land Tax Rating Act 2000, the Land Tax Regulations 2021, the Local Government
-- (Rates and Charges Remissions) Act 1991 and the Local Government (Rates and Charges Remissions) Regulations 2024 --
-- shared nouns for the seat-neutral core.
--
-- This module holds the arithmetic and date helpers, the financial year, the explicit "not covered" answers, and the
-- parties and steps of every regulative rule in lta-core.l4 and rcr-core.l4. It states no rule of any of the five
-- instruments.
--
-- Source: the deposited texts at ../../registers/source-bundle/act-2000-074.txt and in the four sibling subjects
-- (land-tax-rating-act-2000, land-tax-regulations-2021, local-government-rates-and-charges-remissions-act-1991,
-- local-government-rates-and-charges-remissions-regulations-2024). Copyright State of Tasmania, CC BY 4.0. Based on
-- material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 20 October 2026. For the latest information on Tasmanian
-- Government legislation please go to www.legislation.tas.gov.au.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Conventions. A financial year runs from 1 July to 30 June and is named by the year in which it BEGINS: 2026 is the
-- financial year beginning on 1 July 2026 (2026-27). Money is in Australian dollars. Areas are in square metres.

§ `Shared nouns -- Tasmanian land tax and the pensioner rates remission`

§§ `Arithmetic`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `amounts` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total of` MEANS sum `amounts`

§§ `Dates and the financial year`

-- The prelude has no ordering on DATE, so days are compared by their serial numbers.
GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
YearMonthDay `y` `m` `d` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY `d` `m` `y` -- renamed from YMD so it cannot collide with the YMD in newer daydate libraries; see docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md section 5

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is before` `the day` `other` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `other`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `other` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is on or before` `the day` `other` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `other`

GIVEN `first` IS A DATE, `last` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days from` `first` `to` `last` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `last` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `first`

-- A day on or after 1 July falls in the financial year that began on that 1 July; a day from 1 January to 30 June falls
-- in the financial year that began on the previous 1 July.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the financial year of` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day` AT LEAST 7
    THEN DATE_YEAR `the day`
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS 1

-- "the commencement of the financial year" (Land Tax Act s 10(1)); "1 July in the financial year" (Remissions Act
-- s 4(1A)).
GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`1 July of` MEANS YearMonthDay `the financial year` 7 1

-- "the end of that financial year" (Remissions Act s 4(9)).
GIVEN `the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`30 June ending` MEANS YearMonthDay (`the financial year` PLUS 1) 6 30

§§ `Answers outside the deposited texts`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the financial year begins before 1 July 2026: sections 13 and 37 of the Land Tax Act were amended from that day (No. 19 of 2026) and the earlier wording is not in the deposited consolidation`
    `the financial year begins before 1 July 2024: the maximum remission for it is set by regulations that are not deposited (the 2024 Regulations start from 2024-25)`
    `a Hobart CPI figure that the year's maximum remission needs was not given`
    `an owner of this general land may be a foreign person liable to foreign investor land tax (Land Tax Act Division 1A; Land Tax Rating Act s 6A: 2% of the assessed land value, on top of the Schedule 1 amount), which is not encoded`
    `some of the land is exempt, wholly or partly, on a ground other than s 19(a)-(b) (ss 19(ba)-(e), 19A-19E, 29, 30A), and those exemptions are not encoded`

-- An amount of money, or the reason it cannot be worked out from the deposit.
DECLARE `Amount answer` IS ONE OF
    `the amount, in dollars, is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Regulative rules -- the parties and the steps`

-- The parties the five instruments name. The Commissioner of State Revenue and the municipality (the council) are
-- parties to rules, never seats.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the owner`
    `the Commissioner`
    `the applicant`
    `the municipality`
    `the person given the remission`
    `the objector`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `pay the land tax`
    `pay the instalment`
    `pay the full amount of the land tax for the year`
    `notify the Commissioner in writing of the change`
    `lodge a statutory declaration stating the interest in the land`
    `apply for the s 37 rebate`
    `grant a rebate equal to the land tax paid`
    `apply for the s 37A rebate`
    `grant a rebate of the land tax paid on the other land`
    `apply to the municipality for the remission`
    `remit 30% of the rates and charges, up to the prescribed maximum`
    `notify the municipality in writing`
    `make a statement known to be false or misleading`
    `repay the amount remitted`
    `lodge a written objection with the Commissioner`
    `determine the objection and give written notice`
    `apply to the Magistrates Court for a review`
